---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — The Ritz Menu Guide"
  description="About The Ritz Menu Guide: independent, original guides to dining at The Ritz London, by Firoz Khan of FK Digital Media."
  path="/about/"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">About</h1>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6 items-start rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <img
        src="/images/firoz-khan.webp"
        alt="Firoz Khan"
        class="w-28 h-28 rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-gold shrink-0"
      />
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Firoz Khan</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-gold-dark font-medium mt-1">FK Digital Media</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft text-sm leading-relaxed">
          I'm Firoz Khan, an independent maker behind FK Digital Media. I build small, focused
          websites — calculators, guides, and tools — that answer one question well instead of
          everything poorly.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm">
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/firoz-khan-1153358a/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">LinkedIn</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/fkdigitalmedia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://www.instagram.com/rtibyfiroz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Instagram</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide mt-8">
      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        The Ritz Menu Guide publishes independent, original guides to dining at The Ritz
        London — the restaurant's menus, afternoon tea, realistic prices, and how to book.
        Each guide explains what's on the menu, what it costs, what we'd order, and how to
        plan a visit — written in our own words from officially reported facts.
      </p>
      <h2>What this site is not</h2>
      <p>
        We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to The Ritz London. We don't
        reprint menus and we don't copy anyone's photos — every illustration on this site is
        original artwork, and every description is our own writing. Where we link to the
        hotel's own pages and menu PDFs, we say so clearly.
      </p>
      <h2>On prices</h2>
      <p>
        Restaurant prices change with the seasons. We date every price we publish (currently
        from official Ritz sources, August–October 2026), and we ask you to verify with the
        hotel before visiting. We'd rather show an honest dated figure than a false precise
        number.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
